<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="benchmark-cohort" content="october18-corrected-two-items"><title>Decision results by function and load</title><style>body{max-width:1260px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px 80px;background:#f8fafc;color:#193047;font:17px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}h1{font-size:2.35rem;line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:2.3rem;line-height:1.3}a{color:#087f8c}img{max-width:100%;height:auto;background:white;border-radius:10px}table{display:block;overflow-x:auto;max-width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.86rem;margin:20px 0}th,td{border-bottom:1px solid #d5dfe9;padding:9px 11px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#e6eef5}code{font-size:.85em;overflow-wrap:anywhere}pre{overflow:auto;background:#e6eef5;padding:16px}nav{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;border-bottom:1px solid #d5dfe9;padding-bottom:16px;font-size:.9rem}p{max-width:100ch}
.metric-cell{font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap;color:#193047}
.band-1{background:#d8f1e8}.band-2{background:#fff4c2}
.band-3{background:#ffe4ca}.band-4{background:#fbdedd}
.metric-unknown{background:#e7eaee;color:#193047}
.cost-incomplete{text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:dotted;text-decoration-color:#9a6700;text-underline-offset:.25em;border-bottom:2px solid #bd820c}
.legend-note{font-size:.9rem}main{min-width:0}table{overscroll-behavior-x:contain}
@media(max-width:640px){body{padding:18px 12px 56px}h1{font-size:1.8rem}th,td{padding:8px}table{font-size:.8rem}nav{gap:10px}}
</style></head><body><nav><a href="index.html">Overall comparison</a><a href="functions.html">Functions and load</a><a href="output_compliance.html">Output diagnostics</a><a href="three_model_reference.html">Original three-model reference</a><a href="https://github.com/etsabary/jev-1.14-comparison-benchmark">Repository and evidence</a></nav><main><h1 id="results-by-function-and-load-level">Results by function and load level</h1>
<p>The <a href="index.html">main report</a> compares 36 eligible configurations on the corrected 1,136-question bank, tested October 15, 16 and 18, 2026. Each configuration combines 1,134 retained cases and two freshly tested corrected questions; all core scores are unchanged. Every cell uses strict first-attempt results. Unranked full runs, stopped samples and failed interfaces remain in the <a href="output_compliance.html">output diagnostics</a>, not these tables. The 640 core scenarios and 496 dependent variants are not 1,136 independent observations.</p>
<h2 id="what-the-question-types-mean">What the question types mean</h2>
<p>These short illustrations explain the task families. They are not additional scored questions or answer-key entries. Every actual item supplies its own rules, facts and five choices.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Family</th>
<th>What the model has to do</th>
<th>Simple illustration</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>F01 Record lookup and filtering</td>
<td>Select records that meet stated conditions</td>
<td>Which listed request is both signed and marked urgent?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F02 Forward conditional reasoning</td>
<td>Apply an implication from its trigger</td>
<td>If an active badge grants entry and this badge is active, what follows?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F03 Necessary conditions and contraposition</td>
<td>Reason backward from a missing required condition</td>
<td>Every approved request needs a valid ticket; can one without a ticket be approved?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F04 Boolean scope and exclusivity</td>
<td>Track combinations such as both, either and exactly one</td>
<td>Which choice satisfies exactly one of two stated conditions?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F05 Quantifiers and set relations</td>
<td>Track all, some, none and overlapping groups</td>
<td>All teal tokens are marked; no marked token is blank; which relation follows?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F06 Transitive comparisons</td>
<td>Combine ordered comparisons</td>
<td>A is taller than B and B than C; how do A and C compare?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F07 Scheduling constraints</td>
<td>Fit events around order and exclusion rules</td>
<td>Which timetable puts one meeting before another without overlapping a break?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F08 One-to-one assignments</td>
<td>Give each item a unique partner while satisfying clues</td>
<td>Assign three people different desks using location restrictions.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F09 Exact truth counting</td>
<td>Count precisely how many statements hold</td>
<td>Under the supplied facts, how many of six claims are true?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F10 Truth-teller consistency</td>
<td>Find a consistent pattern of truthful and false statements</td>
<td>Which assignment of honest and dishonest speakers fits their claims?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F11 Sufficiency and inconsistency</td>
<td>Determine whether facts force an answer or contradict one another</td>
<td>Is a proposed arrangement determined, impossible or still underdetermined?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F12 Object tracking through swaps</td>
<td>Update locations after repeated exchanges</td>
<td>A red token starts in box A; several box contents are swapped; where does it end?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F13 Sequential procedure execution</td>
<td>Apply each ordered edit to the current state</td>
<td>Toggle one flag, swap two values, then conditionally reset another flag.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F14 Temporal interval relations</td>
<td>Compare starts, ends and overlapping periods</td>
<td>Which interval overlaps a specified event without containing it?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F15 Verbal spatial tracking</td>
<td>Update position or direction from described movement</td>
<td>Follow successive turns and moves, then identify the final direction.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F16 Nested role and reference binding</td>
<td>Resolve chains of names, roles and references</td>
<td>Identify the mentor of the colleague named in a nested description.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F17 Perspective and belief tracking</td>
<td>Distinguish what different observers witnessed</td>
<td>An object moves while one observer is absent; where will that observer look?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F18 Deterministic causal intervention</td>
<td>Recompute consequences of changing a specified input</td>
<td>Force a switch off while holding other inputs fixed; which lamp now lights?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F19 Exceptions and priority rules</td>
<td>Apply a rule, its exception and stated precedence</td>
<td>A badge permits entry unless a higher-priority suspension applies.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F20 Planning with preconditions</td>
<td>Choose an action sequence whose requirements are met</td>
<td>Obtain a key before opening a locked door, with limited moves available.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F21 Directed reachability</td>
<td>Follow arrows in their permitted direction</td>
<td>Can node A reach node D through the listed directed links?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F22 Deterministic preference ordering</td>
<td>Rank candidates using explicit tie-break rules</td>
<td>Rank by priority first, then age when priorities tie.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F23 Rule verification and counterexamples</td>
<td>Find a case that violates a stated rule</td>
<td>Which listed record disproves the claim that every approved item is signed?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F24 Source authority and stale records</td>
<td>Select the valid source rather than an outdated conflicting one</td>
<td>Two records disagree; which controls under the stated authority and date policy?</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>F25 Deterministic fault diagnosis</td>
<td>Match observed symptoms to explicit fault rules</td>
<td>Which fault is consistent with the supplied test results?</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
